Subject: Put the engine identity in the profile header and refuse a mismatch

What this does
  The `.qjsprof` header now carries the register-format version and the build
  configuration beside the ABI, and the generator refuses a profile whose ABI or
  register format does not match the engine it was built with.

Why we need it
  A profile is keyed by a function digest, which is a hash of its register
  bytecode. That bytecode depends on the engine version and on how the function
  was lowered, so a profile from another engine matched nothing and said
  nothing -- the build silently compiled nothing and the app ran slowly with no
  explanation.

What it adds
  `fmt=`, `drc=`, `thr=` and `rec=` in the header; `parse_profile` checks `abi`
  and `fmt`; `profmerge.py` checks and re-emits the format.

Needs a bytecode version bump
  No.

diff --git a/quickjs.c b/quickjs.c
index fe8e2cc..46d051f 100644
@@ -59742,7 +59742,9 @@
         if (!f)
             f = stderr;
     }
-    fprintf(f, "qjsprof 1 abi=%u\n", QJS_AOT_ABI);
+    fprintf(f, "qjsprof 1 abi=%u fmt=%u drc=%u thr=%u rec=%u\n",
+            QJS_AOT_ABI, REGVM_FORMAT_VERSION, QJS_DRC,
+            QJS_REGVM_THREAD, QJS_REGVM_RECORD);
     list_for_each(el, &rt->gc_obj_list) {
         JSGCObjectHeader *gp = list_entry(el, JSGCObjectHeader, link);
         if (JS_GC_TYPE(gp) == JS_GC_OBJ_TYPE_FUNCTION_BYTECODE)
